    "title": "West Virginia receives over $1 million for criminal history improvement program - Charleston Leader",
    "text": "Governor Patrick Morrisey has announced the allocation of $1,107,129 in National Criminal History Improvement Program (NCHIP) funds to support state agencies and the judiciary in West Virginia. The funding aims to enhance the criminal justice system’s efficiency.\nThe U.S. Department of Justice, Office of Justice Programs, Bureau of Justice Assistance provided these funds. The Justice and Community Services Section within the West Virginia Division of Administrative Services is responsible for administering them.\nThe West Virginia Supreme Court of Appeals received $757,129. According to the announcement, “Funds will be used to continue to provide accurate, complete, and timely dispositions that are immediately accessible by allowing law enforcement and court recordkeeping systems to exchange information and make this information available upon criminal history background checks.”\nAdditionally, the West Virginia State Police were awarded $350,000.",
